      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/90 leading-relaxed mt-3 mb-3">
        Video generation models make movies. World models make decisions. Photon-1 is the first commercial proof that you can build a world simulator from <strong>unlabeled screen recordings</strong>. The bet is that action labels are unnecessary overhead, and next-state prediction alone teaches an agent how to act.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/90 leading-relaxed mb-0">
        Induction Labs has not proven it conclusively. Internal benchmarks from a 2-person YC startup are not proof. But 0.47 MAE on billiard physics from a model that only watched desktop recordings? <strong>That is a data point worth watching.</strong>
      </p>
